From: d1-riscv-arch-image-builder
Subject: [PATCH] binman: use importlib.resources instead of pkg_resources

pkg_resources was removed in setuptools 81, so binman fails to even import on
a current Arch container:

  File "tools/binman/control.py", line 16, in <module>
      import pkg_resources
  ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pkg_resources'
  make: *** [Makefile:1124: .binman_stamp] Error 1

control.py already imports importlib.resources and uses it elsewhere, as does
tools/buildman/main.py; these two call sites were simply left behind. Note that
'etype' has no __init__.py, so it has to be reached as a subdirectory of the
binman package rather than as a package in its own right.

diff --git a/tools/binman/control.py b/tools/binman/control.py
index c6d3205b..ee8c8238 100644
--- a/tools/binman/control.py
+++ b/tools/binman/control.py
@@ -13,7 +13,6 @@ except ImportError:  # pragma: no cover
     # for Python 3.6
     import importlib_resources
 import os
-import pkg_resources
 import re
 
 import sys
@@ -96,7 +95,8 @@ def _ReadMissingBlobHelp():
             msg = ''
         return tag, msg
 
-    my_data = pkg_resources.resource_string(__name__, 'missing-blob-help')
+    my_data = (importlib.resources.files('binman')
+               .joinpath('missing-blob-help').read_bytes())
     re_tag = re.compile('^([-a-z0-9]+):$')
     result = {}
     tag = None
@@ -151,7 +151,8 @@ def GetEntryModules(include_testing=True):
     Returns:
         Set of paths to entry class filenames
     """
-    glob_list = pkg_resources.resource_listdir(__name__, 'etype')
+    glob_list = [item.name for item in
+                 importlib.resources.files('binman').joinpath('etype').iterdir()]
     glob_list = [fname for fname in glob_list if fname.endswith('.py')]
     return set([os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(item))[0]
                 for item in glob_list
